  title: 'Past Perfect Tense',
  subtitle: "O'tgan zamonning o'tgan zamoni — birinchi bo'lib sodir bo'lgan harakat",
  level: 'B1',
  day: 60,
  formulas: [
    { label: 'Affirmative (Ijobiy)', structure: 'I/You/He/She/It/We/They + had + V3 (past participle)', color: 'green' },
    { label: 'Negative (Inkoriy)', structure: "I/You/He/She/It/We/They + hadn't + V3", color: 'red' },
    { label: 'Question (Savol)', structure: 'Had + I/you/he/she/it/we/they + V3?', color: 'blue' },
  ],
  rules: [
    "1️⃣ QACHON ISHLATILADI?\n\nPast Perfect — o'tgan zamonning o'tgan zamoni, ya'ni ikki o'tgan harakatdan BIRINCHI sodir bo'lganini ko'rsatish uchun ishlatiladi.\n\n📌 Ketma-ketlik (Sequence): Ikkala harakat ham o'tmishda sodir bo'lgan, birinchisi ikkinchisidan oldin.\n  → I had eaten dinner when he arrived. (Men ovqat yegan edim, u kelgan paytda)\n  → She had finished her work before she left. (U ishini tugatgan edi, ketishdan oldin)\n\n📌 By the time bilan: Biror vaqtgacha qandaydir ish tugagan bo'lsa.\n  → By the time we got to the station, the train had already left. (Vokzalga borgunimizcha, poyezd ketib bo'lgan edi)\n  → By 5 PM, I had finished all my homework. (Soat 5 ga qadar uy vazifamni tugatgan edim)\n\n📌 Reported speech (o'zlashtirma gap): Simple Past → Past Perfect\n  → She said: 'I loved him.' → She said that she had loved him.\n  → He said: 'I went to London.' → He said that he had gone to London.\n\n📌 Never/ever bilan tajriba (Past Perfect): O'tmishdagi bir nuqtadan oldin hech qachon...\n  → She had never seen such a beautiful beach before that trip. (U bu safargacha bunday go'zal plyajni hech ko'rmagan edi)\n  → Had you ever tried sushi before you went to Japan? (Yaponiyaga borishdan oldin sushi yeganmidingiz?)",
    "2️⃣ QANDAY YASALADI?\n\nIjobiy: had + Past Participle (V3)\n  I had finished. / She had gone. / They had seen.\n  → All subjects (I, you, he, she, it, we, they) — hammasi HAD bilan bir xil!\n\n  Regular verbs: V3 = V + ed\n    finish → finished, work → worked, play → played\n\n  Irregular verbs (eng muhimlari):\n    go → gone (borgan edi)      eat → eaten (yegan edi)\n    see → seen (ko'rgan edi)    write → written (yozgan edi)\n    take → taken (olgan edi)    give → given (bergan edi)\n    have → had (ega bo'lgan edi)  make → made (yasagan edi)\n    know → known (bilgan edi)   find → found (topgan edi)\n\n  🔥 MUHIM: Had + V3 — subyekt bilan o'zgarmaydi! I had, she had, we had — hammasi bir xil.\n    ❌ I have finished (Present Perfect bilan almashtirilgan) ❌\n    ✅ I had finished (Past Perfect — to'g'ri) ✓",
    "3️⃣ INKOR SHAKLI (Negative)\n\n  hadn't + V3 (hadn't = had not)\n  I hadn't finished. / She hadn't gone. / They hadn't seen.\n\n  🔴 MUHIM: hadn't dan keyin V3 asl shaklida qoladi!\n    ❌ She hadn't went ❌ (V2 emas! V3 kerak)\n    ✅ She hadn't gone ✓\n\n  Misollar:\n    I hadn't eaten breakfast before the meeting. (Yig'ilishdan oldin nonushta qilmagan edim)\n    She hadn't finished her project when the deadline came. (Muddat kelganda, u loyihasini tugatmagan edi)\n    They hadn't arrived by the time the concert started. (Konsert boshlangan vaqtda ular hali kelmagan edi)\n\n  🔥 Never bilan: NOT ishlatilmaydi! had + never + V3\n    I had never seen such a beautiful sunset. (Hech qachon bunday go'zal quyosh botishini ko'rmagan edim)\n    ❌ I hadn't never seen ❌ (double negative — noto'g'ri)",
    "4️⃣ SAVOL SHAKLI (Questions)\n\n  Had + subject + V3?\n  Had you finished? / Had she gone? / Had they seen?\n\n  Qisqa javoblar:\n    Had you eaten? → Yes, I had. / No, I hadn't.\n    Had she left? → Yes, she had. / No, she hadn't.\n\n  WH-savollar:\n    What had you done before I called? (Men chaqirishdan oldin nima qilgan edingiz?)\n    Where had she gone before the party? (Ziyofatdan oldin u qayerga ketgan edi?)\n    Why had they left so early? (Nega ular buncha erta ketishgan edi?)\n\n  🔥 Past Perfect savollari: odatda 'before' yoki 'by the time' bilan birga keladi.\n    Had you ever visited London before you moved there? (Ko'chishdan oldin Londonda bo'lganmidingiz?)",
    "5️⃣ VAQT BELGILARI (Time Expressions)\n\n  Past Perfect bilan ishlatiladigan eng muhim vaqt belgilari:\n\n  📌 BEFORE — oldin\n    I had finished my work before he arrived. (Ishimni u kelishdan oldin tugatgan edim)\n    She had left before I called. (U men chaqirishdan oldin ketgan edi)\n\n  📌 AFTER — keyin\n    After I had finished dinner, I went for a walk. (Kechki ovqatni tugatgach, sayrga chiqdim)\n    After she had studied, she took a nap. (O'qib bo'lgach, u dam oldi)\n\n  📌 BY THE TIME — ...gacha\n    By the time we arrived, the movie had already started. (Biz borgunimizcha, film boshlanib ketgan edi)\n    By 6 PM, I had completed all my tasks. (Soat 6 ga qadar barcha topshiriqlarni bajargan edim)\n\n  📌 ALREADY — allaqachon\n    She had already left when I got there. (Men borganda u allaqachon ketgan edi)\n    They had already eaten by the time I arrived. (Yetib kelganimda ular allaqachon ovqatlanishgan edi)\n\n  📌 NEVER / EVER — hech qachon\n    I had never tried such food before. (Oldin bunday taomni hech sinab ko'rmagan edim)\n    Had you ever been to Europe before that trip? (Bu safargacha Yevropada bo'lganmidingiz?)",
    "6️⃣ O'ZBEKCHA FARQLAR (Uzbek vs English)\n\n  O'zbek tilida '-(i)b edi' qo'shimchasi bilan ifodalanadi:\n    'Men ovqat yegan edim' → Past Perfect ✓\n    'U kelgan edi' → Past Perfect ✓\n\n  O'zbek tilida ko'pincha 'oldin', 'keyin' so'zlari bilan aniq bo'ladi, ammo ingliz tilida zamon aniq ko'rinishi KERAK!\n\n  O'zbeklarning eng keng tarqalgan xatolari:\n    • I had went before you called ❌ → I had gone before you called ✓ (V3 ishlatiladi!)\n    • She had ate dinner when I arrived ❌ → She had eaten dinner when I arrived ✓\n    • By the time he came, I had finish ❌ → By the time he came, I had finished ✓\n    • I hadn't never seen that before ❌ → I had never seen that before ✓ (double negative emas!)\n    • After I finished, I left (tushunarli, lekin: After I had finished, I left — to'g'riroq)\n\n  🔥 FARQ: Past Perfect vs Simple Past\n    When she arrived, I cooked dinner. (U keldi, keyin men ovqat pishirdim — ketma-ket)\n    When she arrived, I had cooked dinner. (Men ovqat pishirgan edim, u keldi — birinchi pishirganman)",
    "7️⃣ REPORTED SPEECH — Past Perfect bilan o'zlashtirma gaplar\n\n  O'zlashtirma gapda (reported speech) Simple Past va Present Perfect → Past Perfect ga o'zgaradi:\n\n  📌 Direct speech (to'g'ridan-to'g'ri):\n    He said: 'I love you.' (present)\n    She said: 'I went to Paris.' (past)\n    They said: 'We have finished.' (present perfect)\n\n  📌 Reported speech (o'zlashtirma) — fe'l o'tgan zamonda bo'lsa:\n    He said that he loved her. (present → past — o'zgarmaydi)\n    She said that she had gone to Paris. (past → past perfect)\n    They said that they had finished. (present perfect → past perfect)\n\n  🔥 SODDA QOIDA: Direct speechda ishlatilgan Present Perfect yoki Simple Past, reported speechda Past Perfect ga o'zgaradi.\n\n    'I have never been to London.' → She said she had never been to London.\n    'I bought a car.' → He said he had bought a car.\n    'We saw the movie.' → They said they had seen the movie.\n\n  🔴 LEKIN: Agar reported speech fe'li hozirgi zamonda bo'lsa (says), zamon o'zgarmaydi:\n    He says: 'I went to London.' → He says he went to London. (o'zgarmaydi!)",
  ],
